{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191884": {
      "title": "Associate Athletic Director for Development",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University: Office of the President: Intercollegiate Athletics  Location: Charleston, IL Eastern Illinois University (EIU) invites applications for the position of Associate Athletic Director for Development. This is an exciting opportunity for an energetic, entrepreneurial, and relationship-driven leader to help shape the future of Panther Athletics through philanthropic support, corporate partnerships, and innovative revenue-generating initiatives. Reporting directly to the Director of Athletics, the Associate Athletic Director for Development serves as the department's chief external fundraising officer and is responsible for developing and implementing a comprehensive strategy to expand philanthropic giving, strengthen corporate partnerships, increase premium revenue opportunities, and cultivate long-term financial support for EIU Athletics. The successful candidate will build meaningful relationships with alumni, donors, businesses, and community leaders while identifying creative opportunities to diversify and grow athletic department revenues. The successful candidate will be a collaborative, relationship-driven leader with a demonstrated record of revenue generation success and a commitment to advancing the mission of Eastern Illinois University and Panther Athletics through philanthropy, strategic partnerships, and innovative revenue generation. Primary Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive fundraising and revenue generation strategy that supports the strategic priorities of EIU Athletics, including annual giving, major gifts, planned giving, capital initiatives, and other philanthropic efforts. Cultivate, solicit, and steward relationships with alumni, donors, corporate partners, community leaders, and other stakeholders to expand private support and external revenue opportunities. Identify, develop, and manage corporate sponsorships, premium seating, special events, hospitality, licensing, and other initiatives that generate sustainable revenue and enhance the visibility of Panther Athletics. Collaborate with the Director of Athletics, University Advancement, the EIU Foundation, coaches, and campus partners to establish fundraising priorities, coordinate donor engagement, and pursue innovative revenue opportunities, including NCAA-compliant NIL-related initiatives. Direct donor stewardship, fundraising events, prospect management, reporting, and performance metrics while ensuring compliance with NCAA, conference, university, foundation, and applicable state regulations. Represent EIU Athletics in cultivating strategic relationships with alumni, donors, corporate partners, and community organizations while promoting the mission and goals of Panther Athletics. About Panther Athletics EIU is home to 19 sponsored NCAA Division I teams and roughly 500 student-athletes dedicated to excellence in the classroom and in competition. With a student body of approximately 8,000, the university serves as a vibrant hub of athletic and academic achievement in the region. Over the past 5 years, EIU has made significant facilities investments including structural, aesthetic, and competitive upgrades to O’Brien Stadium, launching Volleyballs Gardella Family Court at McAfee, and Frost Field at Coaches Stadium. The University and Community: Celebrating more than 130 years of excellence, Eastern Illinois University (EIU) is a fully accredited, comprehensive regional residential institution located in Charleston, Illinois—ideally positioned between Chicago, St. Louis, and Indianapolis. The University is known for its individualized attention, supportive relationships, and exceptional outcomes, including high graduation, retention, and career placement rates. Academically, EIU combines personalized learning with nationally respected programs. Small class sizes allow for close mentorship from distinguished faculty, while innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and firsthand opportunities prepare students for meaningful professional and personal growth. Campus life at EIU is vibrant and community oriented. The University features more than 50 buildings within walking distance, extensive recreational facilities, and more than 200 student organizations including NCAA Division I athletics, and 20+ fraternities and sororities. Cultural life thrives at the world-renowned Doudna Fine Arts Center and the Tarble, which bring exceptional artistic and performance experiences to campus and the region. Students, faculty, and staff enjoy the close-knit atmosphere of a classic college town with convenient access to shops, dining, and outdoor recreation—alongside robust service opportunities coordinated through EIU’s Office of Civic Engagement and Volunteerism. With its strong alumni network, sustainability efforts, and deep commitment to student success, Eastern Illinois University offers an exceptional environment to live, learn, and work. Salary and Benefits Final offer will be commensurate with experience and academic credentials.  The position is budgeted for a range of $77,500-$82,500 per year. This is a 12-month position eligible for the following benefits: Comprehensive Medical Coverage: Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. Vision Insurance: Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. Dental Insurance: Dental plans available to meet your needs. Retirement Benefits: Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children. Generous Paid Time Off: Up to 12 paid holidays annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For more information on our employee benefit programs, please visit EIU Employee Benefits webpage. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Three years of progressively responsible experience in fundraising, advancement, development, corporate relations, sponsorship sales, business development, or a related field. Demonstrated success in securing philanthropic gifts, sponsorships, or other revenue-generating partnerships. Excellent communication, interpersonal, organizational, and project management skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required; valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Experience in NCAA Division I fundraising, corporate sales, or university advancement. Demonstrated success securing major gifts, corporate sponsorships, or capital campaign support. Experience working with university foundations, donor CRM systems, and fundraising analytics. Knowledge of NCAA regulations and experience developing innovative external revenue initiatives. To apply for this position, please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for five professional references including name, phone number and email, to https://apply.interfolio.com/191872 . Inquiries, nominations, and questions regarding this search, may be directed to Mark Bonnstetter, Search Committee Chair, at mdbonnstetter@eiu.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194998": {
      "title": "Dean, College Liberal Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University Location: Charleston The College of Liberal Arts & Sciences invites applications for the position of Dean. The Dean will lead the academic college and a faculty who are passionate about their students and committed to innovation. The College of Liberal Arts & Sciences includes 5 schools and 7 departments and is the largest college at Eastern Illinois University. The college is comprised of the departments of Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Psychology, Political Science & Philosophy, Geosciences, Sociology, Anthropology & Criminology, History and the Doudna Fine Arts Center. And the schools of English & World Languages, Communication, Journalism & Theatre, Music, Art & Design (w/Tarble Museum of Art), and Engineering, Mathematics, Computer Science & Physics. The Dean is expected to balance the need to strategically identify new program opportunities and advocate for continued investment in existing academic programs Salary Range: $150,000 - $156,996 per year Benefits Overview: Eastern Illinois University offers an excellent benefit package designed to support our employees’ well-being and career goals. This position is eligible for the following benefits: Comprehensive Medical Coverage : Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. Vision Insurance: Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. Dental Insurance: Dental plans available to meet your needs. Retirement Benefits : Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children. Generous Paid Time Off: Up to 12 paid holidays annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For more information on our employee benefit programs, please visit EIU Employee Benefits webpage. The University and Community: Celebrating more than 130 years of excellence, Eastern Illinois University (EIU) is a fully accredited, comprehensive regional residential institution located in Charleston, Illinois—ideally positioned between Chicago, St. Louis, and Indianapolis. The University is known for its individualized attention, supportive relationships, and exceptional outcomes, including high graduation, retention, and career placement rates. Academically, EIU combines personalized learning with nationally respected programs. Small class sizes allow for close mentorship from distinguished faculty, while innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and firsthand opportunities prepare students for meaningful professional and personal growth. Campus life at EIU is vibrant and community oriented. The University features more than 50 buildings within walking distance, extensive recreational facilities, and more than 200 student organizations including NCAA Division I athletics, and 20+ fraternities and sororities. Cultural life thrives at the world-renowned Doudna Fine Arts Center and the Tarble, which bring exceptional artistic and performance experiences to campus and the region. Students, faculty, and staff enjoy the close-knit atmosphere of a classic college town with convenient access to shops, dining, and outdoor recreation—alongside robust service opportunities coordinated through EIU’s Office of Civic Engagement and Volunteerism. With its strong alumni network, sustainability efforts, and deep commitment to student success, Eastern Illinois University offers an exceptional environment to live, learn, and work. Non-discrimination, EEO/AA Statement: Eastern Illinois University provides equal opportunity in education and employment for all students, applicants for employment, and employees. Discrimination based upon race, color, sex, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, marital status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis of discrimination precluded by federal and state statutes, is strictly prohibited. The University further commits to a program of affirmative action as prescribed by statute to employ, and advance in employment, qualified individuals with a disability and qualified protected veterans (disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active-duty wartime veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans). The successful candidate for this position will have: A terminal degree with a record of teaching, research, service, and expertise appropriate for a tenured faculty appointment in an academic department within the College At least five years of increasingly progressive administrative duties including three years as a department chairperson or higher A record of collaboration across academic departments and disciplines Experience with and commitment to discipline and profession-specific accreditation An appreciation for and understanding of the unique role of a regional comprehensive institution situated in east-central Illinois A commitment to advancing the mission of the college through fundraising and expanded external relationships with community and industry partners Applicants must submit a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and contact information for three references to https://apply.interfolio.com/194998 . Questions about the application process should be directed to Dr. Jill Hutti, Screening Committee Chair, Academic Affairs, 217-581-6348, jrrennelshutti@eiu.edu . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled with priority given to applications received prior to Friday, October 30, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193063": {
      "title": "Director Human Resources",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University: Business Affairs: Business Affairs Location: Charleston Eastern Illinois University is seeking applications and nominations for a highly motivated and experienced administrator to serve as the University’s Director of Human Resources. The Director reports to the Vice President for Business Affairs and has primary responsibilities for the administration and leadership of a comprehensive human resources department. Areas of responsibilities include all phases of employment for civil service employees, including efforts to achieve diversity within the workplace; employee training and professional development; participation in collective bargaining process; contract administration; position classification and compensation; and benefits for all university employees. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Leading, administering, coordinating and supervising all aspects of programs and activities for civil service employees in the following areas: recruitment, screening, testing, interviewing, employment, orientation, compensation and classification, training and development, performance appraisals, and maintenance of electronic files for employees Leading, administering, coordinating and supervising all aspects of programs and activities for all employees in the following areas: employee benefits, workers compensation, unemployment compensation, Family and Medical Leave Act administration, and ADA accommodations Providing leadership in maintaining quality staff through recruitment, retention, and professional development, with attention given to achieving diversity in the workplace Providing leadership in the development and implementation of personnel policies and procedures for matters related to employees. Providing leadership and direction for HR information systems to create efficient and customer service-oriented processes Manage unemployment claims and matters Implementing and managing the university background check and MVR process. Managing the desk audit process Serving as financial manager and assuming responsibility for the appropriate use and management of funds for the Human Resources unit Serving as the University's designated employer representative (DER) of the State Universities Civil Service System Serving as an administrative liaison to the University's Civil Service Council. Coordinating with Employee and Labor Relations on civil service disciplinary issues and other civil service matters. A member of various negotiation teams when requested Assist with development and administration of mandatory training, such as Identity Protection Act training and other training as mandated Represent the University on various external committees Other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Business Affairs. Work Hours: Standard office hours are 8:00am - 4:30pm Benefits Overview: Eastern Illinois University is proud to offer an excellent benefits package designed to support our employees' well-being and career goals. This position is eligible for the following benefits: Comprehensive Medical Coverage: Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. Vision Insurance: Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. Dental Insurance: Dental plans available to meet your needs. Retirement Benefits: Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children after vesting period. Generous Paid Time Off: Up to 12 paid holidays  annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For complete information on our employee benefit programs for this specific position, please visit EIU Employee Benefits webpage The University and Community: Celebrating more than 130 years of excellence, Eastern Illinois University (EIU) is a fully accredited, comprehensive regional residential institution located in Charleston, Illinois—ideally positioned between Chicago, St. Louis, and Indianapolis. The University is known for its individualized attention, supportive relationships, and exceptional outcomes, including high graduation, retention, and career placement rates. Academically, EIU combines personalized learning with nationally respected programs. Small class sizes allow for close mentorship from distinguished faculty, while innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and firsthand opportunities prepare students for meaningful professional and personal growth. Campus life at EIU is vibrant and community oriented. The University features more than 50 buildings within walking distance, extensive recreational facilities, and more than 200 student organizations including NCAA Division I athletics, and 20+ fraternities and sororities. Cultural life thrives at the world-renowned Doudna Fine Arts Center and the Tarble, which bring exceptional artistic and performance experiences to campus and the region. Students, faculty, and staff enjoy the close-knit atmosphere of a classic college town with convenient access to shops, dining, and outdoor recreation—alongside robust service opportunities coordinated through EIU’s Office of Civic Engagement and Volunteerism. With its strong alumni network, sustainability efforts, and deep commitment to student success, Eastern Illinois University offers an exceptional environment to live, learn, and work. Nondiscrimination and AA/EEO Statement: Eastern Illinois University is committed to fostering a learning community where all members feel welcomed and valued. The university provides equality of opportunity in all areas of campus life, and we strive to recognize and appreciate the unique value of our students, faculty, and staff. Every member of campus has the right to learn and work in an environment free of discrimination and harassment, and beyond that, our goal is for all members of our community to develop a strong sense of belonging to Eastern Illinois University. Eastern Illinois University provides equal opportunity in education and employment for all students, applicants for employment, and employees. Discrimination based upon race, color, sex, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, marital status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis of discrimination precluded by federal and state statutes, is strictly prohibited. The University further commits to a program of affirmative action as prescribed by statute to employ, and advance in employment, qualified individuals with a disability and qualified protected veterans (disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active-duty wartime veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans). Information for Applicants: Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act to complete the application and/or interview process. If would like to request assistance with the application/interview process, please contact Human Resources at (217) 581-3911 or eiu_employment@eiu.edu for assistance Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources Management, Business, or other related field required Five years of recent applicable human resources experience, with at least 3 in a significant management or leadership role Excellent oral and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree in related field Relevant professional experience in Higher Education Application: Applications must be submitted through the University's “Interfolio\" application system https://apply.interfolio.com/193063 Submitted materials should include: 1) a cover letter addressing the candidate's experience and qualifications as related to the position description; 2) a resume or curriculum vitae describing the candidate's professional work history, education, and other qualifications; and 3) a list identifying the names, addresses, and contact information (phone and email) for three professional references. Review will begin immediately and continue until filled. Candidates are encouraged to submit materials no later than October 9, 2026, for full consideration. For questions regarding the search, contact Michael Hutchinson, Screening Committee Chair at mwhutchinson@eiu.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189322": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University: Lumpkin College of Business and Technology: School of Business Location: Charleston, IL The School of Business at Eastern Illinois University invites applications for a full ‑ time, nine ‑ month, tenure ‑ track position in accounting at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the School’s mission through excellence in teaching, research, and service. Candidates with research and teaching interests in all areas of accounting will be considered. Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate the ability and willingness to teach across accounting areas (e.g., financial accounting, accounting information systems, managerial accounting, auditing, and taxation) and to adapt as departmental needs evolve. We especially seek candidates who already have experience using AI to supplement teaching and to engage students. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses delivered in face ‑ to ‑ face, online, and hybrid formats. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate is expected to maintain a sustainable research program that generates scholarly output consistent with the missions of the School of Business and the Accountancy Program. An established or emerging record of publication in peer ‑ reviewed journals is required. While traditional academic research is valued, applied and pedagogical research are also encouraged. The position also involves service to the School of Business and the University. A demonstrated passion for teaching, student mentoring, and overall student career development is highly valued. Salary Range: $126,000 - $157,500 Benefits Overview: Eastern Illinois University is proud to offer an excellent benefits package designed to support our employees' well-being and career goals. This position is eligible for the following benefits: · Comprehensive Medical Coverage: Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. · Vision Insurance: Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. · Dental Insurance: Dental plans available to meet your needs. · Retirement Benefits: Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. · Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children. · Generous Paid Time Off: Up to 12 paid holidays annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For more information on our employee benefit programs, please visit EIU Employee Benefits webpage Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Accounting from an AACSB ‑ accredited accounting doctoral program with a strong record of research training in accounting. Candidates who are ABD and close to completion will be considered. Evidence of strong instructional effectiveness and excellent communication and interpersonal skills are required. Professional certifications such as CPA, CMA, or other relevant designations are a plus. Business experience and experience teaching online are also desirable, particularly when accompanied by a strong grounding in U.S. GAAP, demonstrated fluency with the FASB Accounting Standards Codification, and familiarity with related U.S. regulatory and reporting standards. To successfully apply, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research philosophy, and the names and contact information (including phone numbers and email addresses) for three references. Applications must be submitted electronically via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/189322 . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until all preliminary interviews are scheduled. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Stu Sallehu, Search Committee Chair, at mmsallehu@eiu.edu . Employment is contingent upon verification of eligibility to work in the United States. Immigration sponsorship, if needed, will be considered in accordance with applicable law, University policy, budget resources, and review by the University’s immigration counsel. The University may be unable to support extraordinary expenses."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182290": {
      "title": "Instructor, School of Nursing",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University: College of Health and Human Services: Gail and Richard Lumpkin School of Nursing Location: Charleston, IL The School of Nursing at Eastern Illinois University invites applications for two full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track faculty positions at the rank of Instructor, with an anticipated start date of August 2026. We seek candidates committed to excellence in student learning and to the academic and clinical education of undergraduate nursing students in the traditional prelicensure BSN and RN-BSN programs. Responsibilities include classroom, laboratory, and clinical instruction; student mentoring; participation in program assessment and curriculum development; and service to the School, College, and University. The vision of the School of Nursing is to promote health and well-being through innovative, concept-guided, and interprofessional education; cultivate high-quality nursing practice; serve diverse local and global populations; and instill a commitment to lifelong learning. The School of Nursing offers a fully online RN-BSN program and a traditional prelicensure BSN program. Faculty collaborate to provide high-quality educational experiences for both online and on-campus students. Duties Teach in the undergraduate traditional BSN and online RN-BSN programs Provide classroom, laboratory, and clinical instruction Assist with preparation, maintenance, and implementation of nursing laboratory activities Mentor and advise students Participate in curriculum development and program assessment Engage in service at the program, college, and university levels Maintain RN licensure and engage in professional development and continuing education Contribute to faculty governance Travel to clinical sites as required Perform other duties as assigned Benefits Overview: Eastern Illinois University is proud to offer an excellent benefits package designed to support our employees' well-being and career goals. This position is eligible for the following benefits: Comprehensive Medical Coverage: Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. Vision Insurance: Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. Dental Insurance: Dental plans available to meet your needs. Retirement Benefits: Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children. Generous Paid Time Off: Up to 12 paid holidays annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For more information on our employee benefit programs, please visit EIU Employee Benefits webpage. Diversity and Inclusion Eastern Illinois University is committed to fostering a learning community where all members feel welcomed and valued. The university provides equality of opportunity in all areas of campus life, and we strive to recognize and appreciate the unique value of our students, faculty, and staff. Every member of campus has the right to learn and work in an environment free of discrimination and harassment, and beyond that, our goal is for all members of our community to develop a strong sense of belonging to Eastern Illinois University. Eastern Illinois University provides equal opportunity in education and employment for all students, applicants for employment, and employees. Discrimination based upon race, color, sex, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, marital status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis of discrimination precluded by federal and state statutes, is strictly prohibited. University and Community Celebrating more than 130 years of excellence, Eastern Illinois University (EIU) is a fully accredited, comprehensive regional residential institution located in Charleston, Illinois—ideally positioned between Chicago, St. Louis, and Indianapolis. The University is known for its individualized attention, supportive relationships, and exceptional outcomes, including high graduation, retention, and career placement rates. Academically, EIU combines personalized learning with nationally respected programs. Small class sizes allow for close mentorship from distinguished faculty, while innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and firsthand opportunities prepare students for meaningful professional and personal growth. Campus life at EIU is vibrant and community oriented. The University features more than 50 buildings within walking distance, extensive recreational facilities, and more than 200 student organizations including NCAA Division I athletics, and 20+ fraternities and sororities. Cultural life thrives at the world-renowned Doudna Fine Arts Center and the Tarble, which bring exceptional artistic and performance experiences to campus and the region. Students, faculty, and staff enjoy the close-knit atmosphere of a classic college town with convenient access to shops, dining, and outdoor recreation—alongside robust service opportunities coordinated through EIU’s Office of Civic Engagement and Volunteerism. With its strong alumni network, sustainability efforts, and deep commitment to student success, Eastern Illinois University offers an exceptional environment to live, learn, and work. Required: Current or eligibility for Registered Nurse licensure in Illinois by start date Master’s degree in Nursing Clinical preparation and experience in medical-surgical and/or psychiatric nursing Minimum of two years of clinical practice experience Willingness to teach within a concept-based curriculum and complete professional development in concept-guided education Commitment to student-centered teaching and ability to adopt instructional technologies Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty and administrators Preferred: Experience teaching in an accredited nursing program Online teaching experience Candidates must meet Eastern Illinois University qualifications for online teaching, established through prior distance education training/experience or successful completion of the EIU Online Course Development Institute: https://www.eiu.edu/fdic/online.php . Submit application materials to Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/182290 . Inquiries about the position may be directed to Dr. Andrew Kirkley, Screening Committee Chair, adkirkley@eiu.edu . Review of completed applications will begin March 23, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. A complete application includes: Letter of application addressing qualifications and responsibilities of the position Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references who can speak to relevant clinical and/or academic teaching experience"
    }
